      "episode_id": "dandelion-pr13947",
      "proposal": "Dandelion / BIP156 transaction origin privacy",
      "venue": "GitHub PR",
      "technical_objections": [
        {
          "text": "we still need to figure out what the right behavior is for transaction chains and replacement transactions \u2026 and generally how to prevent DoS attacks during stem routing",
          "source": "github",
          "answered": "",
          "basis": "",
          "cite": "ee24474a93a3a82c72028970ab5b9cda8b76c37da670170fbd24b8b703750066"
        },
        {
          "text": "If we use a stempool \u2026 I'm not sure I understand how we could share a stempool across multiple inbound peers without leaking dandelion routing information to an adversary",
          "source": "github",
          "answered": "",
          "basis": "",
          "cite": "ee24474a93a3a82c72028970ab5b9cda8b76c37da670170fbd24b8b703750066"
        },
        {
          "text": "Neither `dandeliontx` or `dandelionacc` are mentioned and/or specified in the BIP.",
          "source": "github",
          "answered": "",
          "basis": "",
          "cite": "d7c99966b47748e485ba9efb5c569b9d37e8393c7871f181a8cc673cc92d32ff"
        }
